WEBVTT

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.643
Let's...

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.270
take that bath together.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.313
What?!

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:22.397
TOP SECRET MISSION

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.608
This is my grandma's writing.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.526
-What is this?
-Izana!

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:27.903
Let go of me!

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.074
Watch out, be careful!

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:34.910
Nagate, you don't care about me at all!

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.162
What? Of course I care about you!

00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:42.751
EMERGENCY REQUEST

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.835
Command Division?

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:45.921
Pardon?

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.131
Yes, understood.

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:54.096
Someone was arrested for deserting
tomorrow's reconnaissance mission.

00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:56.431
And I guess I was the next in line.

00:00:58.225 --> 00:01:00.852
We're taking too long switching
to the type 2 equipment!

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:03.021
It may be recon,
but they're going onto the battlefield!

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:05.607
Hurry up and drop
maintenance stations four and five!

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:07.067
They're in the way!

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.570
<i>Units have been outfitted
<i>in their type 2 equipment.</i></i>

00:01:09.653 --> 00:01:12.739
<i>Pilots, board your units after
<i>they've been cleared for deployment.</i></i>

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:18.328
<i>Planet Nine Reconnaissance Team
<i>has been deployed.</i></i>

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.581
<i>Suspension device locked.</i>

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:22.583
<i>Launch gate, course secured.</i>

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.876
<i>High-speed support armor Hayakaze,</i>

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.336
<i>ready for deployment!</i>

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.630
Launch the Hayakaze!

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:42.686
<i>Hayakaze, begin docking approach.</i>

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:46.315
Get ready!

00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:56.033
That's right, slowly now.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:03.040
Linkage successful!

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:09.129
We are passing by the planet's rings.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.132
There's a haze in our flight course.

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:13.925
I'll try firing
the Heigus particle cannon.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.554
There's something there!

00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:19.431
What is that?!

00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:26.521
<i>Go forth and conquer!
<i>Let there be light!</i></i>

00:02:30.525 --> 00:02:35.822
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:42.579
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.750
KNIGHTS OF SIDONIA

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:56.676
<i>Our only haven is this fortress</i>

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.763
<i>Wandering among the stars</i>

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:03.016
<i>Where we tremble with impatience</i>

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.435
<i>Between life and death</i>

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:11.191
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:16.029
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:24.162
<i>Those of us who have been led
<i>To gather here</i></i>

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:30.877
<i>Carry within ourselves the will to fight</i>

00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:34.506
<i>Our lives shine their brightest</i>

00:03:34.589 --> 00:03:37.008
<i>In the defense of love</i>

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.971
<i>We boldly enter the fray</i>

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:45.475
<i>The Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:55.485
ENTRY

00:03:58.113 --> 00:03:59.656
It's a cloaked gauna!

00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:02.284
Recon Team, eject from Hayakaze.
You have to evade it!

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.835
MAN-MADE KABI LOST
PENETRATION FAILED

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.140
No, the membrane is growing.

00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:30.562
We've lost Unit 640!

00:04:31.813 --> 00:04:33.732
What about the other units?!

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:36.443
<i>512, 723, you all right?!</i>

00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:38.570
<i>-Yes, sir!
<i>-I made it somehow.</i></i>

00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:45.786
Multiple gauna signals detected
closing in from the sides!

00:04:48.163 --> 00:04:49.456
<i>They're shooting at us!</i>

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:55.587
We've lost Unit 512!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.590
-Unit 064 suffered minor damage!
-What about the other units?!

00:04:59.341 --> 00:05:00.425
Recon Team, respond!

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:03.553
There is heavy communication interference.
We're reconfirming their positions!

00:05:04.846 --> 00:05:08.642
Units 064 and 723
have entered the atmosphere!

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:10.894
We've lost communication!

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:15.982
More gauna cores detected!

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.568
They seem to have multiplied suddenly!

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.446
Captain...

00:05:22.364 --> 00:05:23.824
Planet Nine will be

00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:26.701
a crucial strategic point
in our war with the gauna cluster.

00:05:27.953 --> 00:05:31.206
Midorikawa, form a plan to eliminate
the gauna from Planet Nine.

00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:34.960
But we need to send in rescue teams now.

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:38.088
I didn't order a rescue.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.923
I ordered an extermination.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.345
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:48.014
No... no!

00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:51.977
What?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.228
Damn it!

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.565
So, the Recon Team has been left to die?

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.942
It's a difficult call to make.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:04.072
Tsumugi, calm down!

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:06.575
No, let me go help them!

00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:09.953
-Izana is in danger!
-Yuhata!

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.873
<i>Oh, I mean,
<i>Probationary Subcommander Midorikawa,</i></i>

00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:16.710
<i>please let us deploy!</i>

00:06:16.918 --> 00:06:17.794
<i>I beg you!</i>

00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:19.462
Tanikaze...

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:21.172
What do you expect exactly?!

00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:24.217
I can't go around following
everybody's own personal requests!

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:28.179
<i>Calm down, Tsumugi!</i>

00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:30.265
<i>I'm concerned</i>

00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:32.934
<i>that we will lose control of Tsumugi</i>

00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:35.854
<i>if Unit 723's pilot dies.</i>

00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:39.524
Damn it. What are they doing?!

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:45.572
<i>May I have a word, Chief Sasaki?</i>

00:06:46.114 --> 00:06:48.992
Kunato, what is it?

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:52.370
<i>I understand that Toa Heavy Industries
<i>has all but completed work</i></i>

00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.706
<i>on the Upgraded Tsugumori 2.</i>

00:06:55.498 --> 00:06:56.791
So, what?

00:06:57.375 --> 00:07:01.004
<i>Commander, we are only facing
<i>common gauna units,</i></i>

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.214
<i>nothing that is a significant threat
<i>to us.</i></i>

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:06.343
<i>It's the perfect opportunity
<i>to gather combat data</i></i>

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:09.012
<i>before our battle with the gauna cluster.</i>

00:07:09.888 --> 00:07:12.223
<i>We should test the capabilities
<i>of the hybrid</i></i>

00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:13.683
<i>and Upgraded Tsugumori 2 in combat.</i>

00:07:15.185 --> 00:07:17.646
Can it be done, Sasaki?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.900
<i>I'll make it work.</i>

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:26.863
Damn it!

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:33.078
Okay, good! Yeah, over there, too!

00:07:35.205 --> 00:07:36.957
Tsugumori 2.

00:07:37.916 --> 00:07:39.250
They completed the upgrade.

00:07:41.086 --> 00:07:42.921
No time to fine-tune it!

00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:45.423
Use your intuition to make
the necessary adjustments!

00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:53.807
Oh, Pilot Tanikaze,

00:07:53.974 --> 00:07:55.392
do you have a moment?

00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:59.646
This unit is significantly lighter
than the previous Tsugumoris.

00:08:00.438 --> 00:08:03.942
I'm sure it handles quite differently
than what you're used to.

00:08:04.526 --> 00:08:06.778
And since you'll probably
be going into combat in gravity...

00:08:06.861 --> 00:08:09.197
Okay! Thank you.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:14.494
But I've done several thousand hours
of training under similar conditions.

00:08:14.577 --> 00:08:15.954
I think I'll be okay.

00:08:16.955 --> 00:08:20.333
All right! Send out
the Upgraded Tsugumori 2!

00:08:26.423 --> 00:08:29.300
We were dangerously close
to Tsumugi losing control.

00:08:30.385 --> 00:08:33.430
You haven't changed, Kobayashi.

00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:02.208
STANDBY DEPLOYMENT

00:09:04.586 --> 00:09:06.588
Mozuku, Tsumugi!

00:09:06.671 --> 00:09:08.214
What's your condition?

00:09:15.722 --> 00:09:17.849
We're fine.

00:09:40.872 --> 00:09:43.166
This is Tsumugi, I'm ready when you are.

00:09:53.468 --> 00:09:55.178
Tanikaze, deploying!

00:10:01.726 --> 00:10:03.728
Hybrid, deploying.

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:31.381
Tsumugi, get ready for clasp formation!

00:10:31.756 --> 00:10:32.715
Okay!

00:10:37.178 --> 00:10:38.805
<i>Izana...</i>

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:41.015
<i>We're coming for you.</i>

00:11:09.294 --> 00:11:13.590
<i>The Hayakaze's armor partitions should
<i>shield the heat from atmospheric entry.</i></i>

00:11:13.673 --> 00:11:15.300
<i>It's going to work.</i>

00:11:25.894 --> 00:11:29.272
<i>Entering the atmosphere
<i>to escape the gauna...</i></i>

00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:31.608
<i>Not a bad idea, Shinatose.</i>

00:11:31.691 --> 00:11:35.194
I wouldn't be so sure. It seems like
the gardes are at their limit.

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:43.786
<i>They're catching up to us!</i>

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.154
Oh, no! The Ballistic Acceleration Device!

00:12:23.826 --> 00:12:26.287
<i>The Ballistic Acceleration Device.</i>

00:12:27.205 --> 00:12:29.874
<i>The gauna are drawn
<i>to the man-made kabi rounds.</i></i>

00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:34.295
<i>But... all of the gauna
<i>we've ever encountered</i></i>

00:12:34.462 --> 00:12:37.256
<i>didn't stop attacking gardes
<i>without Kabizashis.</i></i>

00:12:42.804 --> 00:12:44.180
I've got it!

00:12:47.392 --> 00:12:48.643
EJECTION NOT RECOMMENDED

00:12:52.105 --> 00:12:53.022
EJECTING

00:12:59.654 --> 00:13:02.198
<i>What the hell are you doing, Shinatose?!</i>

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.574
<i>Did you just dump our fuel?!</i>

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.284
Yes.

00:13:05.368 --> 00:13:07.870
The gauna are most likely
tracing the kabi

00:13:07.954 --> 00:13:09.998
and the high concentration
of Heigus particles.

00:13:10.206 --> 00:13:11.499
<i>What?</i>

00:13:13.918 --> 00:13:17.422
Look! The gauna have stopped chasing us!

00:13:29.851 --> 00:13:32.979
Oh, I guess you were right.

00:13:33.271 --> 00:13:35.898
But without fuel...

00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:38.526
I'll use our remaining electricity

00:13:38.609 --> 00:13:40.653
to glide us out as far as we can.

00:14:10.641 --> 00:14:16.439
SITES OF SIDONIA
ALLEY IN ADMINISTRATIVE REGION

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:39.587
Command, have you made contact
with Izana?

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.172
<i>No, still no signal.</i>

00:14:42.173 --> 00:14:46.260
<i>We have no idea what happened after
<i>they entered Planet Nine's atmosphere.</i></i>

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:54.727
Tanikaze, I'm sure Izana is okay!

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.358
Yeah...

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:03.027
you're right, Tsumugi.

00:15:20.711 --> 00:15:24.298
All right, we're almost to the point
where we lost contact with Izana.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.967
Get ready to enter the atmosphere!

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.385
WARNING

00:15:28.136 --> 00:15:29.846
<i>Gauna approaching from the front!</i>

00:15:30.388 --> 00:15:32.181
GAUNA PROJECTED CORE LOCATION
COUNTLESS

00:15:32.473 --> 00:15:34.183
Tsumugi, release clasp formation!

00:15:50.533 --> 00:15:52.702
GAUNA DISINTEGRATION COUNTLESS
GAUNA CORE-PIERCING ROUNDS

00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:55.037
Kill confirmed! Form up!

00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:56.080
Okay!

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.482
Those two are perfectly in sync.

00:16:27.904 --> 00:16:29.572
What is it, Tsumugi?

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:33.493
It's nothing. I thought I saw something.

00:16:35.703 --> 00:16:37.997
HEIGUS PARTICLES DETECTED DIRECTLY BELOW
DANGER WARNING

00:17:10.112 --> 00:17:12.281
Tanikaze has crashed down
onto that floating mass!

00:17:12.365 --> 00:17:16.077
Detecting high levels of Heigus particles!
Most likely a Heigus particle cannon!

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.662
The attack originated from the planet!

00:17:17.745 --> 00:17:18.788
Tanikaze...

00:17:18.913 --> 00:17:20.289
Expand the scanning area.

00:17:20.373 --> 00:17:22.250
<i>Trace it back to the original source!</i>

00:17:22.833 --> 00:17:25.753
There's no way he survived that crash.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:27.838
Oh, my God...

00:17:28.089 --> 00:17:29.257
Tanikaze...

00:17:38.099 --> 00:17:40.768
<i>Tanikaze! Tanikaze!</i>

00:17:40.851 --> 00:17:41.769
<i>Come in!</i>

00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:56.200
<i>Tanikaze! Tanikaze!</i>

00:17:56.284 --> 00:17:57.493
<i>Come in!</i>

00:17:58.828 --> 00:17:59.996
Yes!

00:18:00.955 --> 00:18:02.039
I'm alive?!

00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:03.291
And the garde?!

00:18:03.499 --> 00:18:05.251
<i>Working, of course!</i>

00:18:05.418 --> 00:18:06.836
<i>Hurry up and get up!</i>

00:18:09.714 --> 00:18:13.050
TANIKAZE 704 COMMUNICATION INTERFERENCE
NO DAMAGE TO INTERNAL STRUCTURE

00:18:15.761 --> 00:18:17.763
I'm glad it was the new model.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.018
Wow.

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:26.689
How is the unit undamaged
after that crash?

00:18:27.356 --> 00:18:28.733
Pretty amazing, right?

00:18:28.816 --> 00:18:30.943
It may look just like
the Upgraded Tsugumori,

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:34.822
but the armor material and internal
structure are completely different!

00:18:34.905 --> 00:18:36.991
Most of the equipment
made from the old material

00:18:37.116 --> 00:18:38.534
has been destroyed.

00:18:38.993 --> 00:18:42.371
<i>Tanikaze, that new material
<i>saved your life.</i></i>

00:18:42.538 --> 00:18:45.541
<i>The old Upgraded Tsugumori
<i>would be in pieces right now.</i></i>

00:18:45.708 --> 00:18:46.917
<i>Yes...</i>

00:18:47.585 --> 00:18:49.629
There's a lot of interference.

00:18:50.212 --> 00:18:53.883
The atmosphere is generating
heavy communication interference.

00:19:12.318 --> 00:19:13.861
Tsumugi! Where are you?

00:19:15.571 --> 00:19:17.865
HEIGUS PARTICLES DETECTED
IN CLOSE PROXIMITY

00:19:25.623 --> 00:19:26.666
Tsumugi!

00:19:48.145 --> 00:19:49.271
NO SIGNAL DETECTED

00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:01.617
We've reestablished communication
with the hybrid!

00:20:01.909 --> 00:20:05.037
Tsumugi, are you okay?!
What's the situation?!

00:20:05.246 --> 00:20:06.914
Currently engaged with the enemy!

00:20:10.501 --> 00:20:14.171
The gauna is using the islands
as a shield.

00:20:14.714 --> 00:20:16.799
It's demonstrating complete knowledge
of the geography!

00:20:24.473 --> 00:20:26.809
Tsumugi! You need to go higher!

00:20:32.314 --> 00:20:33.190
It didn't work?!

00:20:33.774 --> 00:20:37.027
<i>This gauna...
<i>there's something different about it.</i></i>

00:20:47.788 --> 00:20:49.707
Tanikaze! It went in your direction!

00:21:04.013 --> 00:21:05.973
A red gauna.

00:21:13.189 --> 00:21:17.401
<i>We're checking the gauna's ena
<i>wave signature against our database.</i></i>

00:21:17.818 --> 00:21:20.279
<i>Measuring Heigus particle concentration!
<i>It's higher than other gaunas!</i></i>

00:21:20.571 --> 00:21:24.366
The ena wave signature pattern
matches Gauna 490!

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.455
No...

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.540
The Crimson Hawk Moth.

00:21:31.749 --> 00:21:33.542
Rechecking the signature pattern.

00:21:33.876 --> 00:21:37.588
It's a 95% match!
It's the Crimson Hawk Moth!

00:21:39.006 --> 00:21:40.591
I didn't know it was still alive.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:56.190
Crimson Hawk Moth...

00:22:05.574 --> 00:22:07.284
<i>That should be a direct hit.</i>

00:22:28.556 --> 00:22:29.723
Tanikaze!

00:22:29.807 --> 00:22:32.142
Go to Izana! Hurry!

00:22:40.901 --> 00:22:42.528
TO BE CONTINUED

00:22:46.949 --> 00:22:50.911
<i>Oh, if this world must decay</i>

00:22:50.995 --> 00:22:54.665
<i>And I'm destined to give my life away</i>

00:22:54.748 --> 00:22:59.837
<i>What should I be living for?</i>

00:23:01.422 --> 00:23:05.759
<i>If I had never met you</i>

00:23:05.843 --> 00:23:09.430
<i>I would never have known</i>

00:23:09.513 --> 00:23:15.436
<i>This pain that tears at my heart</i>

00:23:15.519 --> 00:23:17.855
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-Echoing there</i></i>

00:23:17.938 --> 00:23:19.940
<i>-Fortune
<i>-In the furthest reaches of the cosmos</i></i>

00:23:20.024 --> 00:23:22.943
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Is this clumsy requiem</i></i>

00:23:23.027 --> 00:23:25.321
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-And yet</i></i>

00:23:25.404 --> 00:23:27.239
<i>-Fortune
<i>-I'm still searching</i></i>

00:23:27.323 --> 00:23:30.659
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Within this uncertain reality</i></i>

00:23:31.243 --> 00:23:32.745
<i>For you</i>

00:23:32.828 --> 00:23:36.457
<i>The joy of our finding each other</i>

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:40.169
<i>The vanished warmth</i>

00:23:40.252 --> 00:23:43.881
<i>You should know that I remember it all</i>

00:23:43.964 --> 00:23:47.635
<i>Because I loved you</i>

00:23:47.718 --> 00:23:51.305
<i>The emotions that arise</i>

00:23:51.388 --> 00:23:54.933
<i>The scars left in my heart</i>

00:23:55.017 --> 00:23:59.355
<i>You should know that I'll carry them all</i>

00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:06.028
<i>As I walk this path</i>
